WEBVTT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.950
"Port island city of Baleun"

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.950
"Port island administrative building"

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.950
There's more than I expected.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.620
I can't believe they were trying to
smuggle out so much contraband.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.040
They underestimated us.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.160
I mean, your Foreign Affairs Ministry
and our Ministry of Fairies

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.450
inspect all cargo on westbound ships.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.290
I couldn't agree more.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.410
Wh-What's this?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.950
What's the matter?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.330
It can't be...

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.830
There's no way!

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.410
Is it... some kind of banned book?

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.660
The <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.620
I've never seen the real thing,
but if this is authentic...

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.830
Then it's more than we can handle.
We'll have to consult the higher-ups.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.500
"Episode 16"
"Kite Laughing Out Loud"

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:55.750
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:00.580
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:16.500
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.500
Michel Connor?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.080
Bishop Griff Mercer.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.540
"Ministry of Fairies 
Assistant Vice-Minister
and fairy technician: 
Griff Mercer"

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.540
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.580
Archbishop Bellwood.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.370
Bishop Mercer. Has something happened?

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.120
 the ideal world to emerge.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.910
Given the way you're dressed.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:25.160
I apologize for defiling holy ground
with this secular attire.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.580
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.620
No matter. I assume urgency was required.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.160
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.910
Something must have happened, Griff.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.450
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.450
Well...

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:42.700
The <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> was in the cargo of a
trade ship headed west from the port island?

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.540
Those westerners are cunning, all right.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.450
"Minister of Fairies: 
Marco Bellwood"

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.450
If Your Excellency hadn't
based post-unification trade

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:55.290
solely from the port island of Baleun,
our wealth and cultural assets

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.950
probably would have drained
endlessly into the west.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:03.580
Even so, there's no end of those who try to
smuggle contraband out of our empire.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.580
"Prime Minister of Unified Zesskia:
Golbarn Helwise"

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.700
Talk about incorrigible.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:11.540
The Ministry of Fairies will deal with this.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:16.950
Yes, Excellency. I wish to have Dorothea
go to the island and see to it.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.120
Right.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.580
Minister, the rest of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i>
includes <i>Black Three</i> , <i>Black Six</i> ...

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.250
...and <i>Black Nine</i> .

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:35.910
There've long been rumors that <i>Black Three</i> and
<i>Black Six</i> might be in the hands of Gui Carlin.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.830
Then it's <i>Black Nine</i> that was found.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:45.370
There's still no guarantee it's the real thing.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.200
We will soon know.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.450
Yes.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.120
It is all the will of the fairies.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.410
I see, at the port island.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.870
Someone apparently tried
to transport it west, but...

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:02.580
But they got caught during an inspection.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.620
And, news of it reached my old ears.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.750
So it would seem.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.500
See you at the port island.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.790
Yeah.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.200
The <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> ...

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.450
Ver.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.250
Can you do this?

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.450
I've long been afraid of trusting anyone.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.750
Yes, sir!

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:36.950
All right.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:44.750
If I were to trust someone,
bad things would happen,

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:48.000
and it'd be sure to cause trouble for them.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.120
But...

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.500
Or rather, he did it for a <i>comrade</i> .

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:56.000
Can't you trust us?

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:09.000
So, we're going to the port island?

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:10.580
"Businesswoman &amp; Gui Carlin mafia group
associate member: 'Sweetie' Bitter Sweet"

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.580
That's right, Patty.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.540
"Gui Carlin mafia group 
member: Patricia Pearl"

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.540
There's something funny going on.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.580
There sure is.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.040
Looks like this will be a fun drive.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.620
Cleaning time!

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.410
Bye!

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:00.790
Nice one!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.790
I wonder how much they got from Gui Carlin.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:09.000
What would you do if they offered
you twice the amount I paid?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.080
That all depends on Lady Sweet,
the demon queen.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.870
"Demon queen"?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:20.830
Of course, you already paid me a high fee.
That's why I threw in the "Lady" part.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.830
"Port island administrative building"

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.290
Who the hell're you?!

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.700
Wh-Who goes there?!

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.870
Whoa...

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.370
That's horrid.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.370
Looks like someone got here first.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.950
P-Please...

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:12.160
I-I-I'm begging you.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:15.500
Don't kill me. I have a wife and child.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.830
So please... Just spare my life...

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.830
Just spare my life!

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.330
Hey, hurry it up.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.620
Yes, I have it now.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:45.700
I wasn't expecting much, but look
at that. The real <i>Black Nine</i> .

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:48.250
Hand over the book.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.790
"One of the Gui Carlin mafia group's
four top executives: Eajey Daven Thor"

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:55.200
Who're you guys?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.000
You're not... with Unified Zesskia.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:06.450
You must be descendants of Albastora.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.120
Bingo.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:26.450
Well, well. A fairy.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.580
Watch out!

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:38.660
That's a Fairy Weapon!

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.080
You're quick.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.160
Veronica! Be careful!

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.330
Forget it, let's go!

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.540
Veronica!

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:19.290
This <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:24.120
It was Crucia Albastora who wrote it,
but there was in fact source material.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.370
Did you know that?

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:31.160
Colen Thor. He's the fairy scholar
who wrote the <i>White Fairy Tome</i> ,

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:34.120
and my ancestor, as it turns out.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:39.660
Colen Thor explored Midend,
and left behind extensive notes.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.700
You're saying, those n-notes were...

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:47.750
That's right. Crucia Albastora
was Colen Thor's student,

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:52.160
and he took credit for his teacher's
exploits to write the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.160
There's no excusing a bad guy like him.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:03.290
It'd be hard for someone to clean this up alone.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.160
This way!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.200
Damien Carme?

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:19.040
What, an old lover?

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.200
No way.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.790
What if this one really is an ex-boyfriend?

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.790
Eajey.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.370
From Gui Carlin?

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:39.950
I only know his name,
but I hear he's pretty dangerous.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.540
He's one of the four top execs.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:46.040
Huh?! The Eyes, Nose, and Mouth guys?!

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:48.370
You know, he was carrying a book.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.620
Yes, the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.410
It <i>was</i> authentic.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.290
What do we do?

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.250
Free!

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:04.080
What's wrong?

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.580
Something's burning over there!

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.790
What?!

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:11.910
Lily! Seal off the bridge!
Don't let anyone off the island!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:12.910
Understood.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.120
Let's go, Marlya!

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.330
Yes, sir!

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:30.870
Fire!

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:33.160
What's the security force doing?!

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:33.160
A fire?!

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.620
Marlya, you look after the injured!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.160
Yes, sir!

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.910
It's dangerous! Get back! Get back!

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.370
--What's going on?!
--There's a fire?

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.450
--I heard the administrative building's on fire!
--Hurry! Put out the fire!

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:46.620
If that's <i>Black Nine</i> , we have to
dispose of it no matter what.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:52.540
Who is that man, though?
He knows I'm a descendant of Albastora.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.790
Or did he just ask me a leading question,

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.790
knowing I'm trying to get rid
of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> ?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:03.330
Whatever the case... I can't
kill that guy in a fair fight.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.500
Oh!

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.040
If it isn't Damien.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.830
Of all the places to meet.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:13.450
What a coincidence, Bitter Sweet.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.620
Or, perhaps it's inevitable.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:19.370
You're after the
<i>Black Fairy Tome</i> too, aren't you?

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:24.660
I spotted you two at the
administrative building.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.200
After that, Eajey exited, carrying a book.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.160
Eajey? That's the man's name?

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.830
You know who he really is?

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.910
Gui Carlin's Eyes.
One of the four top executives.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.450
He's not my type, though.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:44.700
Gui Carlin... That's why he
wants the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> ?

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.200
Care to fight alongside me?

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:51.290
It sounds like you have the wrong idea.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.830
Yes, all right.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:55.290
We can't trust this woman.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:59.620
Hi!

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.870
Got to have insurance.

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:06.450
Don't you suppose I'm reliable,
when I'm this cautious?

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.540
I'll say.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.120
I'm against this.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.250
Eajey's a tough customer. Let's all get along.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:20.450
As a result of all that, the fire was
put out at the administrative building.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:23.410
It seems the security force
has the bridge blocked,

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:26.870
and even small boats that come
and go are being policed.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.790
Which means, nobody can leave the port island?

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.160
Y-Yes, sir.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:36.910
But even with the aid of our Daven &amp; Co.,
getting off the island would be...

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.450
It doesn't matter.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:40.580
Sir?

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:46.120
I obtained what I was after,
thanks to the info you provided.

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.160
There's no need to rush.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:54.250
Albastora's descendants are
probably still on the island too.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.410
This actually works to my advantage.

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:10.040
You've done well.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.950
Y-Yes, sir... I-I appreciate that.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:15.790
Now, then.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.450
I think I'll go out.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:29.500
Won't you sit down?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.040
Free! Dorothea's here too?!

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.950
Again? Doesn't this mean trouble?

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.790
We'll be fine. I think.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:47.080
I'd like to use whatever I can. Dorothea, eh?

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.290
They don't know who I really am.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:55.950
I'll try making contact. I want information.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.370
See you later.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.200
The administrative building
nearly burned to the ground.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:05.500
Someone made off with the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:08.370
They probably set fire to
the place before leaving.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:12.370
In any case, the culprit should
still be on this port island.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.830
That guy...

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.500
Oh?

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.290
We met in Isharat...

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.250
Mr. Damien Carme, was it?

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.040
Yes, thanks for your help that time.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:29.330
You can pick up rare things on the port island,
so I come here now and then,

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.540
but I've never run into a situation like this.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.620
Maybe that was no ordinary fire after all.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:37.410
If you guys are here, then...

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:41.080
You might not be able to
leave the island for a while.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.950
I suppose not.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:46.700
There's also a rumor a
suspicious man was spotted

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:48.410
near the administrative building that burned.

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.370
A suspicious man?

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.660
Could you fill us in on the details?

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.660
Certainly.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:17:02.500
Well. It's not like that Damien guy
can even use a fairy, right?

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:11.040
He's no good in a fight, so maybe having him
go off to gather information's not a bad idea.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.660
Not that I'd know.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:15.500
Do you have any leads?

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.080
I just might.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.250
Really? You do?

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:24.620
Eajey is well connected with Daven &amp; Co.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:30.000
They're a huge trading firm.
One of their offices is on this island.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.080
Do you plan to investigate there?

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:33.330
For now, I'll--

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:40.080
Huh?!

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.290
What the...?!

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:53.750
You really know how to make an entrance.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:58.080
Albastora. I don't see the man.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:00.870
Instead, the weird women are multiplying.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:05.410
Sweetie... You loose bitch with no moral code.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.450
Don't get me wrong, Eajey.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.750
I'll make a deal anytime with even
Gui Carlin, like I always have.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.540
A deal?

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:18.200
It's my policy to team up with anyone,
if our interests coincide.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.250
I'll be helpful.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:26.910
You want her, don't you?

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:31.080
More like, isn't she the one who wants this?

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:38.910
Albastora. You guys owe me,
and I'm going to get even.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.540
This sounds interesting.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.450
Gui Carlin's Eyes' fairy is his "eyes"...

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:11.120
Just when I thought it was a bad joke...

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.330
Fairy weapon.

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.540
This is way beyond me!

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.950
You damn battle-ax.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.830
I call foul on that Fairy Weapon!

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.000
I make the rules.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:50.830
Morterant, the Fairy Weapon held by the
Seven Knights' Harristan, of Timoon!

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.870
How'd <i>you</i> get ahold of it?!

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:55.700
The War of Unification was fun.

00:19:55.700 --> 00:20:00.370
People died left and right,
and I made quite a profit.

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:02.660
Weren't you a Timoon mercenary?!

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:06.790
You can't play around on the battlefield
unless you pretend to be a mercenary.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.870
You move well, but...

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.290
My only real option is to run!

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.410
Oh?

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.250
Hey!

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:29.200
Look out!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.410
What?

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.500
Ver?!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.250
--Veronica!
--Ver!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.540
How dare you!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.750
A fairy?!

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:44.660
Run!

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:47.370
Don't do it! He has a Fairy Weapon!

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.160
The hell?!

00:20:55.790 --> 00:20:57.450
Take this!

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.790
You're kidding me!

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.540
Dorothea, huh?

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.200
This isn't good.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.000
Ver!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.910
If only I had Verosteal!

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:23.660
I've changed my mind.

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:26.870
If you want <i>Black Nine</i> , come and get it.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.040
If you guys can manage it, that is.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.660
You think we'll just let you get away?!

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:41.620
Yep. That's exactly what you'll do.

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:45.080
What a lowlife!

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:47.950
I'm in luck.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.660
Shit!

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:56.540
Earlier...

00:21:57.870 --> 00:22:00.500
You called out "Veronica."

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.500
Who the hell are you?!

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.200
What are you to Ver?!

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:41.580
I found out where he is.

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:42.200
I'll do what I must.

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:45.000
What do you know?

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:45.000
All the contents of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.000
That's why I can fight.

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.500
"Next time"
"Balance on Sand"

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:47.120
That's why I can fight.

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:48.500
Because I have everyone.
